# CODEOWNERS — who reviews what by default.
#
# PRs touching @jukaLang-owned paths auto-request a review so a new
# contributor's change never lands silent. Keep the root rules broad: review
# follows the default owner until a second active maintainer joins (roadmap
# item 23, contributor ladder).
#
# Sorted so the *last* matching pattern wins — put broader rules above narrow ones.

# Everything defaults to the repo owner.
*                               @jukaLang

# Release engineering gates the release scripts separately from player code.
/release.sh                     @jukaLang
/player/release.sh              @jukaLang
/player/release_sign.go         @jukaLang
/player/tools/                  @jukaLang

# CI and templates change what every PR has to satisfy.
/.github/                       @jukaLang

# The shipped configs are the app's UI: a bad jukaconfig.json ships to every device.
/player/jukaconfig.json         @jukaLang
/player/trimui/                 @jukaLang

# Vendored code stays untouched by bots: Dependabot is pinned to gomod only,
# and any PR here needs the same review as player code.
/player/vendor/                 @jukaLang
